          "path": "_m/g/f/j/c/dundee-contemporary-arts-wp/plaque-on-the-wall-at-dundee-c.jpg",
          "filename": "Plaque on the wall at Dundee Contemporary Arts, Dundee, Scotland.jpg",
          "caption": "Plaque reads:\n\"This historic wall follows the line of the western defences of the Burgh and may also have been part of the Town's Hospital, which existed on this site until it's demolition in the early 19th century. \nThe remains of an 18th centiry well, possible to serve as a private water supply for the hospital, are built into the foundations of the wall at its south-eastern end. \n\nThe lintel dated 1721, now incorporated into the wall, previously spanned the top of the well.\"",
